*> Helpers of the ranged weapon, name tag, bucket and glide tests (lane p46e; COPY after CORETEST and after the test's END PROGRAM, touch the
*> test after changing it):
*>   RT-OPEN USING player row out, connection out, floor y out, cx out, cz out: a standard-tables world (view distance 2, no hostile mobs, difficulty normal) with
*>     Stefan in survival, 9 x 9 stone floor 40 blocks above where he joined (three layers of air above it), standing on it at its centre, noon.
*>   (the registry fixture core/tests/fixtures/ranged-registry is loaded by RT-OPEN)
*>   RT-ITEM-ID USING short item key (PIC X(48), no namespace), item id out
*>   RT-GIVE USING player row, slot (1 based), short item key, count: the slot holds that item (no patch)
*>   RT-ENTITY-ID USING short entity key, entity type id out
*>   RT-COUNT USING entity type id, count out, last row out: the used tracker rows of that type
*>   RT-SPAWN-MOB USING short entity key, dx, dz (FLOAT-LONG from the player), row out: MOB-SPAWN on the floor
*>   RT-CLEAR-SLOTS USING player row: the 36 slots empty
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-OPEN.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY BRWORLD.
 COPY CONTENT.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 65536.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(16) VALUE "Stefan".
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 6.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-BLOCK               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BLOCK-ROW           PIC X(819).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATE-TEXT          PIC X(5).
 01 WS-STATE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-AIR                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-REGISTRY-DIR        PIC X(1100) VALUE "core/tests/fixtures/ranged-registry".
 01 WS-DX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-CONN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-FLOOR                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-CX                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-CZ                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-CONN L-FLOOR L-CX L-CZ.
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE 0 TO CS-HOSTILE-MOBS
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "TEST-STANDARD-TABLES"
     CALL "BR-WORLD-READY"
     MOVE 2 TO BW-DIFFICULTY
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "TEST-JOIN" USING WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH L-CONN
*>   The enchantment registry of the tests (TOOL-ENCHANT-ID reads it): the enchantments of the ranged weapons and the tools.
     CALL "REGISTRY-LOAD-ALL" USING WS-REGISTRY-DIR WS-STATUS
     MOVE CN-PLAYER(L-CONN) TO L-PLAYER
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE(L-PLAYER)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HELD(L-PLAYER)
     MOVE PL-DIM(L-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     MOVE 6000 TO CW-TIME
     MOVE "minecraft:stone" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-BLOCK WS-BLOCK-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-BLOCK-ROW(1 + 4 + 35 + 32 + 288 + 4 + 5:5) TO WS-STATE-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-STATE = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-STATE-TEXT)
     COMPUTE L-CX = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(L-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE L-CZ = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(L-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE L-FLOOR = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Y(L-PLAYER)) + 40
     PERFORM VARYING WS-DX FROM -4 BY 1 UNTIL WS-DX > 4
         PERFORM VARYING WS-DZ FROM -4 BY 1 UNTIL WS-DZ > 4
             COMPUTE WS-X = L-CX + WS-DX
             COMPUTE WS-Z = L-CZ + WS-DZ
             CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-X L-FLOOR WS-Z WS-STATE
             PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 3
                 COMPUTE WS-Y = L-FLOOR + WS-I
                 CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-AIR
             END-PERFORM
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE PL-X(L-PLAYER) = L-CX + 0.5
     COMPUTE PL-Y(L-PLAYER) = L-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE PL-Z(L-PLAYER) = L-CZ + 0.5
     MOVE 1 TO PL-ON-GROUND(L-PLAYER)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-OPEN.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-ITEM-ID.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ITEM-ROW            PIC X(270).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-KEY                  PIC X(48).
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-KEY L-ID.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE FUNCTION TRIM(L-KEY) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY L-ID WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-ITEM-ID.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-GIVE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SLOT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-KEY                  PIC X(48).
 01 L-COUNT                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-SLOT L-KEY L-COUNT.
     CALL "RT-ITEM-ID" USING L-KEY WS-ID
     MOVE WS-ID TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT)
     MOVE L-COUNT TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-VAR(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-GIVE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-CLEAR-SLOTS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 36
         MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(L-PLAYER, WS-I) PL-SLOT-VAR(L-PLAYER, WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-CLEAR-SLOTS.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-ENTITY-ID.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ROW                 PIC X(66).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-KEY                  PIC X(48).
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-KEY L-TYPE.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE FUNCTION TRIM(L-KEY) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY L-TYPE WS-ROW WS-STATUS
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-ENTITY-ID.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-COUNT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-COUNT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-ROW                  BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-TYPE L-COUNT L-ROW.
     MOVE 0 TO L-COUNT L-ROW
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > EN-COUNT
         IF EN-USED(WS-I) = 1 AND EN-TYPE(WS-I) = L-TYPE AND EN-PLAYER(WS-I) = 0
             ADD 1 TO L-COUNT
             MOVE WS-I TO L-ROW
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-COUNT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-SPAWN-MOB.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-KEY                  PIC X(48).
 01 L-DX                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-DZ                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-ROW                  BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-KEY L-DX L-DZ L-ROW.
     CALL "RT-ENTITY-ID" USING L-KEY WS-TYPE
     COMPUTE WS-X = PL-X(L-PLAYER) + L-DX
     MOVE PL-Y(L-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     COMPUTE WS-Z = PL-Z(L-PLAYER) + L-DZ
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING PL-DIM(L-PLAYER) WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW L-ROW
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-SPAWN-MOB.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-PACKET-HEX.
*> USING connection id, packet id, hex out (PIC X(1024)), found out: drains the connection and renders the body (after the packet id, at most 512
*> bytes) of the first packet with that id as lower-case hex; found 0 when there is none (hex "none").
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==PK-==.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 65536.
 01 WS-CLOSE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-THRESHOLD           BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-PACKET-ID           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OUTCOME             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COPY                PIC X(512).
 01 WS-AREA                PIC X(1073741824) BASED.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-WANTED               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-HEX                  PIC X(1024).
 01 L-FOUND                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ID L-WANTED L-HEX L-FOUND.
     MOVE "none" TO L-HEX
     MOVE 0 TO L-FOUND WS-OUTCOME
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PK-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN" USING L-ID PB-BUFFER WS-CLOSE
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-OUTCOME NOT = 0
         CALL "TEST-NEXT-PACKET" USING PB-BUFFER PK-BUFFER WS-THRESHOLD WS-PACKET-ID WS-OUTCOME
         IF WS-OUTCOME = 0 AND WS-PACKET-ID = L-WANTED AND L-FOUND = 0
             MOVE 1 TO L-FOUND
             SET ADDRESS OF WS-AREA TO PK-ADDR
             COMPUTE WS-COUNT = FUNCTION MIN(PK-LENGTH - PK-POS, 512)
             MOVE SPACES TO WS-COPY
             MOVE WS-AREA(PK-POS + 1:WS-COUNT) TO WS-COPY
             CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING WS-COPY WS-COUNT L-HEX
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PK-BUFFER
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-PACKET-HEX.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-CHARGED.
*> USING player row, slot (1 based), count out: the number of projectiles in the charged_projectiles component (type 51) of that slot's stack (0: none).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG VALUE 51.
 01 WS-VALUE               PIC X(64).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOUND               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POS                 BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SLOT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-COUNT                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-SLOT L-COUNT.
     MOVE 0 TO L-COUNT
     CALL "SP-GET-COMPONENT" USING PL-SLOT-VAR(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT) WS-TYPE WS-VALUE WS-LENGTH WS-FOUND
     IF WS-FOUND = 1
         MOVE 1 TO WS-POS
         CALL "SP-VARINT-GET" USING WS-VALUE WS-POS L-COUNT
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-CHARGED.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-ENCHANT.
*> USING player row, slot (1 based), enchantment key (PIC X(112)), level: the stack in that slot gains the enchantment.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HANDLE              BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SLOT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-KEY                  PIC X(112).
 01 L-LEVEL                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-SLOT L-KEY L-LEVEL.
     CALL "TOOL-ENCHANT-ID" USING L-KEY WS-ID
     MOVE PL-SLOT-VAR(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT) TO WS-HANDLE
     CALL "SP-ADD-ENCHANT" USING WS-HANDLE WS-ID L-LEVEL
     MOVE WS-HANDLE TO PL-SLOT-VAR(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-ENCHANT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-DAMAGE.
*> USING player row, slot (1 based), damage out: the durability damage of that slot's stack.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SLOT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-DAMAGE               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-SLOT L-DAMAGE.
     CALL "SP-GET-DAMAGE" USING PL-SLOT-ITEM(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT) PL-SLOT-VAR(L-PLAYER, L-SLOT) L-DAMAGE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-DAMAGE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-CLEAR-TYPE.
*> USING entity type id: removes every tracker row of that type (other than players).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-TYPE.
     CALL "RT-COUNT" USING L-TYPE WS-COUNT WS-ROW
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-COUNT = 0
         CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-ROW
         CALL "RT-COUNT" USING L-TYPE WS-COUNT WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-CLEAR-TYPE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-USE-ITEM-AT.
*> USING connection id, yaw, pitch (FLOAT-SHORT): feeds Use Item (0x43) of the main hand with that look (TEST-USE-ITEM sends yaw 0 and pitch 0).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-PACKET-ID           BINARY-LONG VALUE 67.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-YAW                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 L-PITCH                FLOAT-SHORT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ID L-YAW L-PITCH.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-PACKET-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     CALL "PB-PUT-FLOAT" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-FLOAT" USING PB-BUFFER L-PITCH
     CALL "TEST-FEED-BUFFER" USING L-ID PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-USE-ITEM-AT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-MOTION.
*> USING connection id, found out, vx, vy, vz out (FLOAT-LONG): drains the connection and decodes the first Set Entity Motion (0x67): the entity id is read and dropped, the vector is the
*> motion in blocks per tick (found 0 and the zero vector when none came).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
 01 WS-PACKET              BINARY-LONG VALUE 103.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-CONN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-FOUND                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-VX                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-VY                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-VZ                   FLOAT-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-CONN L-FOUND L-VX L-VY L-VZ.
     MOVE 0 TO L-VX L-VY L-VZ
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-PACKET" USING L-CONN WS-PACKET PB-BUFFER L-FOUND
     IF L-FOUND = 1
*>       TEST-DRAIN-PACKET hands over the packet with its id: the id, then the entity id, then the vector.
         CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID
         CALL "PB-GET-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID
         CALL "PB-GET-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER L-VX L-VY L-VZ
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-MOTION.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-EQUIP-DAMAGE.
*> USING player row, damage out: the durability damage of the stack in the chest slot (MN-EQUIP kind 3).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY CMENU.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-DAMAGE               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-DAMAGE.
     CALL "SP-GET-DAMAGE" USING MN-EQUIP-ITEM(L-PLAYER, 3) MN-EQUIP-VAR(L-PLAYER, 3) L-DAMAGE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-EQUIP-DAMAGE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. RT-JOIN-BOB.
*> USING first player row, bob row out, bob connection out: Bob (survival) joins and stands 3 blocks ahead (+z) of the first player on the same floor, on the ground, alive.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(16) VALUE "Bob".
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PLAYER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-BOB                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-CONN                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PLAYER L-BOB L-CONN.
     CALL "TEST-JOIN" USING WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH L-CONN
     MOVE CN-PLAYER(L-CONN) TO L-BOB
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE(L-BOB)
     MOVE PL-DIM(L-PLAYER) TO PL-DIM(L-BOB)
     MOVE PL-X(L-PLAYER) TO PL-X(L-BOB)
     MOVE PL-Y(L-PLAYER) TO PL-Y(L-BOB)
     COMPUTE PL-Z(L-BOB) = PL-Z(L-PLAYER) + 3
     MOVE 1 TO PL-ON-GROUND(L-BOB)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM RT-JOIN-BOB.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
